## §1 — OBSERVE

### 1.1 Catalogue mechanics (read firsthand)
- Digest §T11: "All states become vertical bars in winner colour; above each solid bar, a dotted column extension shows the losing side's share — 'no state is actually all-red or all-blue' (transcript 2:36). Operation: bar growth + dotted extension; input margin is drawn, per state, before any allocation is discussed (the P-A2 triple: margin → allocation → tally)." Why it works: the film's honesty device — the margin is made visible as physical stuff first, so its erasure is something the viewer has seen. Evidence: ev/t162-margin-bars.jpg · clips/t10-margin-bars.mp4 (156–166 s).
- Style-library techniques-diagrams.md §T212: agrees verbatim (mechanics, window P12 @ 2:37–2:52, evidence, consumer). Tier DESCRIBED — OWED #99. No digest↔register disagreement.
- Transcript anchors (words.json, deduped): 156.75 "But this chart tells a different story / You can see that no state is actually all-red or all-blue." · 163.33 "But almost every state awards its electoral votes the same way…" · 171.78 "If they win the state by 1%, they win 100% of the electoral votes." (the last is T214's rule, spoken over this field's tail).
- Packet gaps: Packet #12 adopted WITH GAPS — G3 (clip-filename offset) touches this item only through the clip name `t10-` serving packet-local T11; the digest entry's explicit citation resolves it. G4 (mechanics thinness on T05/T06/T02/T10 packet-local) does not attach to T11/T212. The census below cures the thinness for this item firsthand.

### 1.2 Evidence frame viewed firsthand
ev/t162-margin-bars.jpg (162 s, sha256 5e5e1fad…22b): the stacked share field — 50 vertical bars, alphabetical Alabama→Wyoming, each bar a 100% stack: dark blue (Dem share) at the bottom, light grey (other) in the middle, red (Rep share) filling to the top; a heavy black horizontal line crosses the field at ≈55% of field height; a yellow hand-drawn arc sweeps under the blue region; state names in rotated serif labels beneath each bar. NOTE: at this instant the field is the STACKED form, not yet the winner-solid + dotted form — the dotted form arrives later in the window (census CP7–CP8). The digest's one-line mechanics compresses two forms of one lifecycle; the recreation implements the full lifecycle the census shows.

### 1.3 Motion census (A10.3 — firsthand, this run)
