35:**Motion findings:** motion instants — sub-second stacked growth at the cut (unresolved at 1 s sampling; allocated, see schedule basis) · annotation draw ≈5000–8000 ms · flatten morph ≈8000–10300 ms · shrink ≈10600–11500 ms · dotted growth ≈11800–14000 ms. Holds — stacked field ≈1000–5000 ms · dotted field 14000 ms→window end. No dissolve anywhere; transitions are morphs/draws.
36:**Dotted-height finding (census-priced, departs from the digest's word "share"):** dotted column heights track the losing side's vote VOLUME, not its percentage share — California's dotted column (loser ≈4.48M votes, T214's priced number) towers over Texas's (loser share higher, volume lower). CONFIG therefore carries a per-state `loserUnits` (relative volume, CA=100) alongside the shares; the technique — losing side drawn as dotted matter above the winner's solid bar — is unchanged.
40:1. State set + order (50 states, alphabetical in the specimen) — labels, per-state Dem/Rep shares (grey = remainder), winner side derived (larger share), per-state loserUnits.
49:10. Dotted extension — dot radius, dot pitch, dots-per-unit scale (count = round(loserUnits × scale)), dot colour rule (winner's colour, per census), growth easing.
63:Nested: `states[50]` — `{label, dem, rep, loserUnits}` with the specimen's approximate 2016 shares (percent; grey = 100−dem−rep): AL 34/62/12 · AK 36/51/2 · AZ 45/49/17 · AR 33/60/7 · CA 61/31/100 · CO 48/43/14 · CT 54/40/9 · DE 53/41/3 · FL 47/49/60 · GA 45/50/25 · HI 62/30/3 · ID 27/59/4 · IL 55/38/28 · IN 37/57/16 · IA 41/51/9 · KS 36/56/7 · KY 32/62/10 · LA 38/58/11 · ME 47/44/4 · MD 60/33/16 · MA 60/32/19 · MI 47/45/24 · MN 46/45/14 · MS 40/57/7 · MO 38/56/15 · MT 35/56/3 · NE 33/58/5 · NV 47/45/8 · NH 47/46/4 · NJ 55/41/22 · NM 48/40/5 · NY 59/36/62 · NC 46/49/27 · ND 27/63/2 · OH 43/51/30 · OK 28/65/9 · OR 50/39/10 · PA 47/48/34 · RI 54/38/3 · SC 40/54/11 · SD 31/61/3 · TN 34/60/15 · TX 43/52/66 · UT 27/45/8 · VT 56/29/2 · VA 49/44/21 · WA 52/36/20 · WV 26/68/4 · WI 46/47/15 · WY 21/67/1. (Shares are specimen values read from the frame + the election the frame depicts; loserUnits are relative volumes, CA=100, priced in §1.3.)
64:Derived (never stored): winner side, grey share, dot count per state = round(loserUnits × dotsPerUnit), completeAtMs, durationMs.
71:Window-start offset: segment-anchored, build 0 ms = source 157000 ms. Departure table: ONE departure — SB-A growth (allocated 0–1488 ms incl. stagger tail) vs CP0 (field present at 0 ms at 1 s sampling): the census cannot resolve sub-second growth, and the clip description names growth as the clip's claim; growth is therefore allocated, and CP0's assertion is the zero-state at t=0 (nothing grown yet) rather than the census frame's settled state. All other checkpoints map 1:1.
73:- CP0 zero: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tGrowMs)` → 0 ms: all bar heights 0, dots 0.
74:- CP1 growth complete: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tGrowMs + CONFIG.growDurMs + CONFIG.growStaggerMs*(states.length-1))` → 1488 ms: CA dem fraction = CONFIG dem share (0.61 of grown height), every bar's dem+grey+rep = 1.
75:- CP2 stacked hold: `stateAt(CONFIG, 4000)` → shares unchanged vs CP1, arcs 0.
76:- CP3 annotation mid: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tArcMs + CONFIG.arcDurMs/2)` → 6400 ms: arc1 progress 0.5, arc2 0.
77:- CP4 flatten mid: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tFlattenMs + CONFIG.flattenDurMs/2)` → 9550 ms: CA winner blend 0.5 (dem segment expanding), labels opacity 0.5.
78:- CP5 flatten complete: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tFlattenMs + CONFIG.flattenDurMs + CONFIG.flattenStaggerMs*(states.length-1))` → 10692 ms: every bar single winner colour, winnerFull=1, line/labels 0.
79:- CP6 shrink complete: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tShrinkMs + CONFIG.shrinkDurMs)` → 11700 ms: stripScale = CONFIG.stripFraction.
80:- CP7 dots mid: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tDotsMs + CONFIG.dotsDurMs/2)` → 12900 ms: first state's dot progress 0.5.
81:- CP8 dots complete: `stateAt(CONFIG, completeAtMs)` → CA dot count = round(100 × dotsPerUnit) = max over states; every count = round(loserUnits × dotsPerUnit).
82:- CP9 hold identity: `stateAt(CONFIG, completeAtMs + 500)` fully equal to CP8 state.
85:- Execute checklist: (1) cut segment.mp4 from source.webm at 156.5–172.5 s (window ±0.5 handles), libx264/yuv420p+AAC faststart, ffprobe filed; (2) build recreation.html (CONFIG at top, pure stateAt, window.__T212 exposed); (3) build comparison.html (shared controls, video.currentTime − 0.5 s handle offset → build ms, labels as charged, phone stacking @media ≤560px); (4) own checks §5 legs 1–3.
86:- Swap test: content — states replaced by a 6-state set {Alpha 70/20/40, Beta 30/55/10, Gamma 52/48/90, Delta 20/70/25, Epsilon 49/51/55, Zeta 80/10/15} (labels/shares/units all change; dot counts + winner colours must follow); timing — `tDotsMs 12000→9000` (CP7/CP8 probe instants move by the CONFIG expressions); palette — `palette.rep #cf4453→#2e9e6b` (observed fill values in stateAt output + renderer binding).
93:- Growth-vs-census timing: SB-A growth is an allocation the census cannot confirm — if the timing lens prices the allocation against CP0, the departure table (§2.3) is the priced answer, filed before the wave.
95:- Flatten stagger tail: CP5's census shows one bar still mid-flatten — stagger is in CONFIG, not hard-coded per bar.
