**Motion findings:** motion instants — sub-second stacked growth at the cut (unresolved at 1 s sampling; allocated, see schedule basis) · annotation draw ≈5000–8000 ms · flatten morph ≈8000–10300 ms · shrink ≈10600–11500 ms · dotted growth ≈11800–14000 ms. Holds — stacked field ≈1000–5000 ms · dotted field 14000 ms→window end. No dissolve anywhere; transitions are morphs/draws.
**Dotted-height finding (census-priced, departs from the digest's word "share"):** dotted column heights track the losing side's vote VOLUME, not its percentage share — California's dotted column (loser ≈4.48M votes, T214's priced number) towers over Texas's (loser share higher, volume lower). CONFIG therefore carries a per-state `loserUnits` (relative volume, CA=100) alongside the shares; the technique — losing side drawn as dotted matter above the winner's solid bar — is unchanged.
**Sub-beats:** SB-A stacked growth (allocated 0–~1500 ms) · SB-B stacked hold + black line + labels · SB-C yellow annotation arcs · SB-D flatten to winner colour (labels/line removed) · SB-E shrink to solid strip · SB-F dotted extension growth · SB-G completed hold.

### 1.4 Variables (§1.3 extraction)
1. State set + order (50 states, alphabetical in the specimen) — labels, per-state Dem/Rep shares (grey = remainder), winner side derived (larger share), per-state loserUnits.
2. Bar geometry — count, pitch, gap ratio, field position/size, baseline.
3. Stacked scale — shares map linearly to field height (100% = full height).
4. Majority line — presence, height fraction (≈0.55 of field height from baseline), colour/width, removal at flatten.
5. Annotation — arc count (2), colour (yellow), width, draw durations/order, arc paths (under-blue sweep, over-red sweep).
6. Timing — growth duration + per-bar stagger, hold, annotation start/duration, flatten start/duration + stagger, shrink start/duration, dots start/duration + stagger, final hold, total duration.
7. Palette — paper ground, Dem blue, Rep red, other grey, line ink, annotation yellow.
8. Flatten rule — segments morph so the winner's colour takes the full bar (loser+grey erased by growth of the winner segment).
9. Strip — final solid strip height fraction of field height.
10. Dotted extension — dot radius, dot pitch, dots-per-unit scale (count = round(loserUnits × scale)), dot colour rule (winner's colour, per census), growth easing.
11. Labels — state-name text, font family/size, rotation angle, fade at flatten.
12. Easing — growth/flatten/shrink easing names.

### 1.5 Guidance dispositions (inline, A9.5)
- A1 §2 typography precedent (runtime sampling of config-rendered text): NOT APPLICABLE — no particle typography; labels are DOM/SVG text rendered from CONFIG `states[].label`, which is the same config-driven principle in its DOM form. Reason stated here per A9.5.
- A5 Owner Cures 1–2 (intensity separation · phrase exclusivity): NOT APPLICABLE as particle/sequence cures — no particle field, no phrase lifecycle. The analogous separation here is construction-level: solid (winner, full opacity) vs dotted (loser, discrete dots) are different *kinds* of mark, never the same mark at two intensities — priced in Plan.
- A5 §4 flow-field model: NOT APPLICABLE — no particle pool exists in this technique.
- Family: diagram/bar-field siblings in Packet #12 (T210 grid-map, T208 dot counts) — bar/field geometry from CONFIG arrays is the family's demonstrated construction; T210's filed lesson (receipt-form discipline, A12/A13) is carried into §5 planning.

## §2 — PLAN

### 2.1 Parameter table (every variable → CONFIG key; specimen value = default)
Top-level: `stageW 640 · stageH 440 · fieldX 32 · fieldTop 28 · fieldH 230 · gapRatio 0.28 · majorityLineFraction 0.55 · majorityLineWidthPx 3 · stripFraction 0.26 · labelFontPx 20 · labelMinPx 20 · labelAngleDeg -55 · dotRadiusPx 2.6 · dotPitchPx 7 · dotsPerUnit 0.26 · tGrowMs 0 · growDurMs 900 · growStaggerMs 12 · tArcMs 5800 · arcDurMs 1200 · arcGapMs 200 · tFlattenMs 8800 · flattenDurMs 1500 · flattenStaggerMs 8 · tShrinkMs 10800 · shrinkDurMs 900 · tDotsMs 12000 · dotsDurMs 1800 · dotsStaggerMs 16 · holdMs 1000 · easing "easeInOut" · palette {ground #f4f1ea, dem #55779e, rep #cf4453, other #c9c9c7, ink #1a1a1a, arc #f2d024, paper #ffffff} · fontFamily "Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif" · title "" (specimen field carries no title)`.
Nested: `states[50]` — `{label, dem, rep, loserUnits}` with the specimen's approximate 2016 shares (percent; grey = 100−dem−rep): AL 34/62/12 · AK 36/51/2 · AZ 45/49/17 · AR 33/60/7 · CA 61/31/100 · CO 48/43/14 · CT 54/40/9 · DE 53/41/3 · FL 47/49/60 · GA 45/50/25 · HI 62/30/3 · ID 27/59/4 · IL 55/38/28 · IN 37/57/16 · IA 41/51/9 · KS 36/56/7 · KY 32/62/10 · LA 38/58/11 · ME 47/44/4 · MD 60/33/16 · MA 60/32/19 · MI 47/45/24 · MN 46/45/14 · MS 40/57/7 · MO 38/56/15 · MT 35/56/3 · NE 33/58/5 · NV 47/45/8 · NH 47/46/4 · NJ 55/41/22 · NM 48/40/5 · NY 59/36/62 · NC 46/49/27 · ND 27/63/2 · OH 43/51/30 · OK 28/65/9 · OR 50/39/10 · PA 47/48/34 · RI 54/38/3 · SC 40/54/11 · SD 31/61/3 · TN 34/60/15 · TX 43/52/66 · UT 27/45/8 · VT 56/29/2 · VA 49/44/21 · WA 52/36/20 · WV 26/68/4 · WI 46/47/15 · WY 21/67/1. (Shares are specimen values read from the frame + the election the frame depicts; loserUnits are relative volumes, CA=100, priced in §1.3.)
Derived (never stored): winner side, grey share, dot count per state = round(loserUnits × dotsPerUnit), completeAtMs, durationMs.

### 2.2 Construction choice
**DOM/SVG bars + dotted extensions (chosen):** one SVG scene; per state a group of three stacked rects (dem/grey/rep) that morph at flatten, a dots group of circles, two annotation paths with dash draw-on, one line, rotated text labels — all geometry from `stateAt(cfg,t)`, a pure function evaluable in node.
Rejected: Canvas 2D — loses per-element ink measurement + DOM label measurement the A6 fit leg needs. CSS keyframes — phase state not evaluable as a pure function (A11 receipts impossible). HTML div bars — 50×(3 segments + ~26 dots) divs are workable but SVG gives exact geometry for harness receipts at less code.

### 2.3 Census-anchor mapping (A10.2) + A11 assertions
Window-start offset: segment-anchored, build 0 ms = source 157000 ms. Departure table: ONE departure — SB-A growth (allocated 0–1488 ms incl. stagger tail) vs CP0 (field present at 0 ms at 1 s sampling): the census cannot resolve sub-second growth, and the clip description names growth as the clip's claim; growth is therefore allocated, and CP0's assertion is the zero-state at t=0 (nothing grown yet) rather than the census frame's settled state. All other checkpoints map 1:1.
Assertions (each: CONFIG expression → evaluated instant):
- CP0 zero: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tGrowMs)` → 0 ms: all bar heights 0, dots 0.
- CP1 growth complete: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tGrowMs + CONFIG.growDurMs + CONFIG.growStaggerMs*(states.length-1))` → 1488 ms: CA dem fraction = CONFIG dem share (0.61 of grown height), every bar's dem+grey+rep = 1.
- CP2 stacked hold: `stateAt(CONFIG, 4000)` → shares unchanged vs CP1, arcs 0.
- CP3 annotation mid: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tArcMs + CONFIG.arcDurMs/2)` → 6400 ms: arc1 progress 0.5, arc2 0.
- CP4 flatten mid: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tFlattenMs + CONFIG.flattenDurMs/2)` → 9550 ms: CA winner blend 0.5 (dem segment expanding), labels opacity 0.5.
- CP5 flatten complete: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tFlattenMs + CONFIG.flattenDurMs + CONFIG.flattenStaggerMs*(states.length-1))` → 10692 ms: every bar single winner colour, winnerFull=1, line/labels 0.
- CP6 shrink complete: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tShrinkMs + CONFIG.shrinkDurMs)` → 11700 ms: stripScale = CONFIG.stripFraction.
- CP7 dots mid: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tDotsMs + CONFIG.dotsDurMs/2)` → 12900 ms: first state's dot progress 0.5.
- CP8 dots complete: `stateAt(CONFIG, completeAtMs)` → CA dot count = round(100 × dotsPerUnit) = max over states; every count = round(loserUnits × dotsPerUnit).
- CP9 hold identity: `stateAt(CONFIG, completeAtMs + 500)` fully equal to CP8 state.

### 2.4 Verification plan (instruments named)
- Execute checklist: (1) cut segment.mp4 from source.webm at 156.5–172.5 s (window ±0.5 handles), libx264/yuv420p+AAC faststart, ffprobe filed; (2) build recreation.html (CONFIG at top, pure stateAt, window.__T212 exposed); (3) build comparison.html (shared controls, video.currentTime − 0.5 s handle offset → build ms, labels as charged, phone stacking @media ≤560px); (4) own checks §5 legs 1–3.
- Swap test: content — states replaced by a 6-state set {Alpha 70/20/40, Beta 30/55/10, Gamma 52/48/90, Delta 20/70/25, Epsilon 49/51/55, Zeta 80/10/15} (labels/shares/units all change; dot counts + winner colours must follow); timing — `tDotsMs 12000→9000` (CP7/CP8 probe instants move by the CONFIG expressions); palette — `palette.rep #cf4453→#2e9e6b` (observed fill values in stateAt output + renderer binding).
- Purity: guards cmd1 grep `segment\.mp4|source\.webm|<video|<img|ajavsMbCapY` → 0 hits; external-reference scan; asset inventory = recreation.html alone.
- A6 legs: fit-table.md (PIL rendered measurement, stand-in font DejaVu Serif named, for the 50 rotated labels + any text) + config-census.md (all literals classified; every CONFIG key incl. `states[]` nested keys resolved to value-flowing sites; CSS-variable check — none used).
- jev-prewave after legs 1–3 + A6, payload per its contract; five-lens wave only on FIRE-WAVE; bar avg ≥85, min ≥70.

### 2.5 Failure points (priced)
- Fitting limits: 50 rotated state labels at phone width — label ink height at 360 px stage must stay ≥11 px (labelFontPx 20 at 640 stage → 11.25 px at 360); longest label "Massachusetts" must fit the label strip diagonally — measured in the fit leg, not asserted.
- Growth-vs-census timing: SB-A growth is an allocation the census cannot confirm — if the timing lens prices the allocation against CP0, the departure table (§2.3) is the priced answer, filed before the wave.
- Dotted-density readability: dot pitch 7 px at 640 stage = 3.9 px at 360 — dots must stay discrete (radius 2.6 → 1.5 px at 360); denser would merge into a solid column and destroy the solid-vs-dotted separation that IS the technique.
- Flatten stagger tail: CP5's census shows one bar still mid-flatten — stagger is in CONFIG, not hard-coded per bar.
- Render-proof limitation: no browser binary in this seat — PIXEL-UNVERIFIED carried to scores.md; comparison page is the render surface.
- Plateau (A2): FIRST ATTEMPT — no prior average; a FAIL files its WHY in scores.md and routes attempt 2 to practice.

