Consumer and working record — T212 §1 Observe, `runs/2026-11-18-cycle-038-wave-35/item-T212-observe-plan.md`, the wave’s `RUN.md`, and `study/recreations/T212-margin-bar-field/`.

1. **The catalogue entries agree with each other, but their evidence covers different phases.** Packet 12 `digest.md` lines 85–89 and `techniques-diagrams.md` lines 381–384 agree on the 2:37–2:52 window, the winner-colour bars with dotted extensions, and both evidence paths. I opened `ev/t162-margin-bars.jpg`. It shows stacked red, grey, and blue shares, rotated state labels, a black line, and a yellow arc. The digest’s description of that still as a field with dotted extensions is incorrect. I also opened `census/census-14000.jpg`, which shows the completed winner-colour strip and dotted columns at the recorded source time of 171 s. Observe has a usable late anchor. The source record would be complete enough to describe the lifecycle once it pairs the early and late frames and binds the flatten, shrink, and dot-growth transitions to archive timestamps. Opening growth remains unresolved in `item-T212-observe-plan.md` §1.3. The packet’s G3 explains the `t10-` filename, and G4 lists packet-local T05, T06, T02, and T10, so it does not cover T11. [Packet gap disposition](</home/hatch/workspace/goals/diy-building-and-real-learning/hidden_files/study-jobs/video-digestion/verdict-history.md:66>)

2. **The dotted phase needs its own data and narration bindings.** Both catalogue entries use “losing side’s share.” The late frame shows that California’s column is taller than Texas’s, consistent with the vote-volume reading in `item-T212-observe-plan.md` §1.3. That comparison and T214’s California figure do not establish the chart’s scaling rule or the per-state `loserUnits` values. Observe can bind the rule with measured dot counts for several states against a named source for vote shares and vote totals, or carry the values as visual estimates. The claim that the dotted margin appears before any allocation discussion also needs narrowing. `digest.md` §T13 places the allocation narration at 163–172 s, and the item’s §1.1 records its onset around 163.33 s, before the recorded dotted phase at 169–171 s. The stacked shares are visible before that narration. The late hold also needs a clean endpoint or an explicit overlap, because §1.3 puts T213’s Minnesota overlay at about 171.5 s, inside the T212 window. [Digest T11–T13](</home/hatch/workspace/goals/diy-building-and-real-learning/hidden_files/study/video-digests/2026-11-17-yt-ajavsmbcapy/digest.md:85>) · [T212 item record](</home/hatch/workspace/goals/diy-building-and-real-learning/hidden_files/study-jobs/recreation/runs/2026-11-18-cycle-038-wave-35/item-T212-observe-plan.md:16>)

3. **The archive passes the pre-cut check.** `ffprobe` measured `source.webm` at 488.301 s with start time 0. The nominal window is `172 − 157 = 15.000 s`. The planned half-second handles yield `172.5 − 156.5 = 16.000 s`, and that interval decoded without errors. `ffprobe` measured the cited clip at 9.966832 s. Its documented 156–166 s placement ends six seconds before the technique window ends and before the dotted phase recorded in §1.3. The cut receipt under command 5 still needs the actual `segment.mp4` probe and its binding to the archive in/out points. [Command 5](</home/hatch/workspace/goals/diy-building-and-real-learning/hidden_files/study-jobs/recreation/guards/guards.md:16>)

4. **There is no prior T212 score to inherit.** The T212 directory contains census files, an empty `codex/` directory, and no `scores.md`. Its ID has no row in recreation `verdict-history.md`. **Lens count: 0.** For T208, `scores.md` lines 18–30, the two filed `jev-prewave` returns, and history line 125 agree on two HOLDs, with own-checks completeness 0.40 → 0.48. **Lens count: 0.** For T210, the Wave 34 score sheet, the two filed returns, and history line 126 agree on two HOLDs, 0.35 → 0.45. **Wave 34 lens count: 0.** Both siblings’ current build hashes match their score sheets. T210’s Cycle 038 completion return subsequently records FIRE-WAVE on that same build, and `codex/lens-motion-cycle038.raw` repeats one hash-bound motion return scoring 72. **Cycle 038 lens count found: 1.** The score sheet and history still show the Wave 34 state, so the newer result is only a partial score. No five-lens average can be computed for either sibling. [Recreation verdict history](</home/hatch/workspace/goals/diy-building-and-real-learning/hidden_files/study-jobs/recreation/verdict-history.md:125>) · [T210 completion return](</home/hatch/workspace/goals/diy-building-and-real-learning/hidden_files/study/recreations/T210-threshold-grid-map/codex/jev-prewave-completion-cycle038.md:372>) · [T210 motion return](</home/hatch/workspace/goals/diy-building-and-real-learning/hidden_files/study/recreations/T210-threshold-grid-map/codex/lens-motion-cycle038.raw:458>)

**Limits** — I viewed the cited still and the filed late census frame and decoded the handled source interval. Exact transition instants, the Minnesota overlay onset, the clip’s source offset, and the dot-to-vote mapping remain unverified firsthand. The T212 build and Observe exit judgment are outside this audit.

